;; A test's own x86-64 assembly (all.T's extra_hc_opts of a .s, CallConv): the file assembled by Arbace's object assembler
;; (bin/repr-asm object, AX4) into an ELF64 relocatable object, which hsi run --asm OBJ loads; a primcall (foreign import
;; prim) of one of its global symbols runs on x86i, Arbace's x86-64 machine (go/arbace/x86i, AX5), in GHC's calling
;; convention for x86-64 (GHC's rts/include/stg/MachRegs.h and the native code generator's assignment): the arguments in R1
;; to R6 (rbx, r14, rsi, rdi, r8, r9) and F1 to F6, D1 to D6 (xmm1 to xmm6, shared by Float# and Double#), Sp in rbp; the
;; procedure returns by jumping to the continuation Sp[0] points to, and its results are read from the same registers.


